## Exclusions

None of the five.

## Pre-1995 hits

**1 of 5:** Leone 1992. Seo 2007, Mokyr 2025, Hopfield 2024, Bennett 2026 are all post-1995.

## Margins under 20%

None. Seo is ~10.6× the 2007 bar. Leone is ~3.4× the 1992 fund100 bar.

## Uncertainties

1. **Seo a3.** Samsung Electro-Mechanics and Daewoo Motors are not biotech. Nexol 1999 is the predecessor; Celltrion Inc. itself is February 2002. I dated a3 to 1999. A stricter reading would use 2002.
2. **Seo a5 pin vs bound.** I pinned 2007 because Mirae says the BMS supply “began generating revenues … in 2007” and JoongAng gives ₩63.5bn that year. I did not find a 2006 dollar figure. If a later reviewer wants a bound, 2002 (founding) to 2007 is a legal 5-year window and still far above the bar at the upper end.
3. **Mokyr a4.** I used the 1976 first book as “independently authored.” Many science rows leave a4 unknown for academics. Flagged as a judgment call in the notes.
4. **Hopfield a3.** Princeton dates Bell Labs as “after graduating” in 1958, not with a separate start-year sentence. Confidence medium.
5. **Bennett a1.** German Wikipedia gives 1954; English Wikipedia marks year of birth missing; Penn/Yale bios do not state a year. I recorded 1954 at **low** confidence rather than unknown. This is the weakest cell in the batch.
6. **Bennett a4.** Spark 2013 is sourced as a scientific co-founding. She is also named as a co-founder of GenSight and Limelight; I did not pin those years. If GenSight predates Spark, a4 would move earlier.
7. **Leone a5.** Sequoia’s own bio dates partner promotion to **1993**; Wikipedia dates VI to **1992**. His Acquired interview still identifies VI as the fund on which he became GP. Confidence medium. If a reviewer required a fund closed after the 1993 promotion, VII 1995 at $250M also clears that year’s $47.3M bar. Wikipedia’s $150M for VI is also in tension with a Thomson/UC compilation that lists VI at $100M; **both** figures still clear $43.6M.

Researched **5 of 5**. No fabricated roster entries. No list-membership failures.
